    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "God Judges the Proud"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "For the choir director. A Maskil of David. When Doeg the Edomite went and reported to Saul, telling him, “David went to Ahimelech’s house.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Why boast about evil, you hero!",
          "God’s faithful love is constant."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Like a sharpened razor,",
          "your tongue devises destruction,",
          "working treachery."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You love evil instead of good,",
          "lying instead of speaking truthfully."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "You love any words that destroy,",
          "you treacherous tongue!"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "This is why God will bring you down forever.",
          "He will take you, ripping you out of your tent;",
          "he will uproot you from the land of the living."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Selah"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The righteous will see and fear,",
          "and they will derisively say about that hero, ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "“Here is the man",
          "who would not make God his refuge,",
          "but trusted in the abundance of his riches,",
          "taking refuge in his destructive behavior.”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But I am like a flourishing olive tree",
          "in the house of God;",
          "I trust in God’s faithful love forever and ever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will praise you forever for what you have done.",
          "In the presence of your faithful people,",
          "I will put my hope in your name, for it is good."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
